# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/

# Secrets and environment.
#
# The negation on the last line is load-bearing: `.env.*` matches `.env.example`,
# so without it the committed template would be silently ignored and every fresh
# clone would have no idea which keys the project wants. Order matters in a
# gitignore - the exception has to come after the rule it overrides.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json
credentials.json

# Local editor / agent settings. Machine-specific, not part of the experiment.
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Simulated outputs.
#
# results.probe.jsonl, sweep_degraded.jsonl and frontier.jsonl are regenerated in
# seconds from a pure hash, so committing them adds nothing reproducible. They are
# ignored for a stronger reason than that: while they hold mock output, every
# number in them is FABRICATED, and a committed file full of plausible percentages
# is the single most likely way a simulated figure gets mistaken for a measured
# one.
#
# results.jsonl is ignored, and as of 7 August 2026 it does not exist: the 47
# real rows that used to sit here were from the 30 July plumbing run, and every
# one of their task ids died in the 6 August task-set rebuild. They are kept,
# unedited, in archive/results.2026-07-30.jsonl - see archive/README.md.
#
# The ignore rule stays so a mock run's output is never staged by accident.
# `git add -f results.jsonl` is the deliberate act that publishes a real run,
# and run_eval.guard_clobber blocks a mock run from overwriting one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results.jsonl
results.probe.jsonl
sweep_degraded.jsonl
frontier.jsonl
results.*.bak

# The per-ladder files scripts/run_all_ladders.py writes. Same rule as the
# unsuffixed names above and for the same reason - `git add -f
# results.claude.jsonl` is the deliberate act that publishes a ladder's run.
results.*.jsonl
frontier.*.jsonl
sweep_degraded.*.jsonl
run_all_ladders.log

# Figures are generated from the jsonl above by plot.py, in seconds, with no
# dependencies. While the inputs are simulated the figures are too, and a chart is
# far more likely than a table to be screenshotted and quoted without its caption.
# Commit them once there is a real run behind them.
figures/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw model-response cache.
#
# cache/raw_calls.jsonl (REAL responses) is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the
# whole point: committing it makes every number in this repo reproducible by
# someone with no API key, via ROUTER_MODE=replay. Commit it after the paid run.
#
# cache/routellm_scores.jsonl is likewise NOT ignored, and committing it is what
# lets the routellm policy run without torch, a checkpoint download, or a GPU.
# As of 7 August 2026 there is no such file: scores are keyed on the prompt, so
# the 6 August rebuild left only 10 of 100 matching and the policy was silently
# sitting out. The old scores are in archive/, and regenerating them against the
# current task set is free and local - `python routellm_router.py --score`.
#
# cache/raw_calls.mock.jsonl (SIMULATED responses) IS ignored. It regenerates for
# free in seconds, so committing it would add half a megabyte of fabricated model
# output to the repo for no reproducibility gain.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One cache file per ladder, so `raw_calls.wide.jsonl` is real and committable
# while `raw_calls.wide.mock.jsonl` is fabricated and ignored.
cache/*.mock.jsonl
cache/*.tmp
cache/*.lock
cache/*.bak

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
